### Staff API Testing - Katwanyaa High School
### Images are optional - you can test without them
@baseUrl = https://katwanyaa.vercel.app/api
@staffEndpoint = {{baseUrl}}/staff

### 1. GET ALL NEWS
GET {{baseUrl}}/news
Content-Type: application/json

### 2. GET ALL EVENTS
GET {{baseUrl}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

### 3. CREATE EVENT 1: SCIENCE FAIR
POST {{baseUrl}}/events
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary123

--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Annual Science & Innovation Expo 2026
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Katwanyaa High School presents its 5th Annual Science Fair showcasing student innovations, robotics demonstrations, and environmental projects.
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="fullContent"

The Annual Science & Innovation Expo 2026 is our flagship event that brings together the brightest young minds from across the region. This year's theme is "Sustainable Solutions for Tomorrow" focusing on climate change mitigation, renewable energy, and smart agriculture technologies.

Featured Exhibitions:
1. Solar-powered irrigation systems developed by Form 4 students
2. AI-assisted learning tools for mathematics
3. Biodegradable plastics from agricultural waste
4. Water purification systems for rural communities
5. Robotics and automation demonstrations

Guest Judges:
- Dr. Emily Njeri (Kenyatta University)
- Prof. Samuel Kimani (JKUAT)
- Eng. David Ochieng (Kenya Power)

Prizes:
🥇 1st Place: KSh 50,000 + Trophy
🥈 2nd Place: KSh 30,000 + Medal
🥉 3rd Place: KSh 20,000 + Certificate

Open to public from 10:00 AM onwards. Media partners: Nation Media Group & Citizen TV.
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="date"

2026-04-15
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="time"

9:00 AM - 5:00 PM
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="location"

School Main Hall & Science Laboratories
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="category"

academic
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="attendees"

all
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="speaker"

Prof. Mary Wanjiku (Head of Sciences)
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="type"

external
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="featured"

true
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="science-fair.jpg"

< ./sample-images/science-fair.jpg
--boundary123--

### 4. CREATE EVENT 2: CAREER DAY
POST {{baseUrl}}/events
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary456

--boundary456
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Career Guidance & University Expo 2026
--boundary456
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Annual career fair featuring 30+ universities, professional associations, and industry experts to guide Form 3 & 4 students.
--boundary456
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="fullContent"

Katwanyaa High School's Career Day 2026 is the largest career guidance event in the county. We bring together universities, colleges, professional bodies, and industry leaders to help students make informed career choices.

Participating Institutions:
- University of Nairobi
- Kenyatta University
- Strathmore University
- Jomo Kenyatta University of Agriculture & Technology
- Technical University of Kenya
- Kenya Medical Training College
- Kenya Institute of Management

Industry Partners:
- Safaricom PLC
- KCB Group
- Kenya Airways
- Microsoft Kenya
- Nation Media Group
- Deloitte Kenya

Workshop Sessions:
1. "Future of Work: Digital Skills for 2030" (10:00 AM)
2. "Scholarships & Financial Aid" (11:30 AM)
3. "Entrepreneurship in Kenya" (1:00 PM)
4. "Study Abroad Opportunities" (2:30 PM)

Registration required for Form 3 & 4 students. Parents are encouraged to attend.
--boundary456
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="date"

2026-04-22
--boundary456
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="time"

8:00 AM - 4:00 PM
--boundary456
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="location"

School Sports Field & Classrooms
--boundary456
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="category"

academic
--boundary456
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="attendees"

students
--boundary456
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="speaker"

Career Guidance Department
--boundary456
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="type"

internal
--boundary456
