### BASE URL

### 1. CREATE NEWS 1: KCSE ACHIEVEMENT
POST {{baseUrl}}/news
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary123

--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Katwanyaa High School Sets New KCSE Record with 85% University Entry
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="excerpt"

Our school celebrates historic performance in 2025 KCSE exams, with 3 students scoring straight A's and 85% qualifying for university.
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Breaking records and setting new standards! Katwanyaa High School has achieved its best KCSE results ever in the 2025 national examinations.
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="fullContent"

## HISTORIC ACHIEVEMENT

Katwanyaa High School has made history in the 2025 Kenya Certificate of Secondary Education (KCSE) examinations, recording the best performance since the school's establishment in 1980.

### KEY STATISTICS:
- **85%** of candidates qualified for university (Mean Score: 8.2)
- **3 students** scored straight A's (A plain)
- **45 students** scored A- and above
- **92%** of students attained C+ and above
- **100%** transition rate to higher education

### TOP PERFORMERS:
1. **Brian Kipchumba** - A (85 points)
   Subjects: Mathematics (A), Physics (A), Chemistry (A), Biology (A), English (A), Kiswahili (A), Geography (A), Business Studies (A)
   
2. **Faith Chebet** - A (84 points)
   Subjects: Mathematics (A), Physics (A), Chemistry (A), Biology (A), English (A), Kiswahili (A), History (A), CRE (A)
   
3. **Samuel Omondi** - A (83 points)
   Subjects: Mathematics (A), Physics (A), Chemistry (A), Biology (A), English (A), Kiswahili (A), Agriculture (A), Computer Studies (A)

### SCHOOL RECOGNITIONS:
- Best Performing School in the County
- Top 10 in National Science Performance
- Best Improvement Award (from 6.8 to 8.2 mean score)

### HEADMASTER'S STATEMENT:
"This remarkable achievement is a testament to the hard work of our students, dedication of our teachers, and support from parents. We are proud to continue our legacy of academic excellence and character formation."

The school will hold a celebration ceremony on April 10, 2026, where top performers will receive scholarships and awards.
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="date"

2026-04-05
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="category"

achievement
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="author"

School Communications Office
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="featured"

true
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="kcse-results.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< /path/to/your/image.jpg
--boundary123--

### 2. CREATE NEWS 2: INFRASTRUCTURE DEVELOPMENT
POST {{baseUrl}}/news
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary456

--boundary456
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

New STEM Center Opens: KSh 50 Million Digital Learning Facility
--boundary456
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="excerpt"

Governor commissions state-of-the-art STEM center with robotics lab, 3D printing facilities, and digital classrooms.
--boundary456
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

A new era of digital learning begins at Katwanyaa High School with the commissioning of our KSh 50 million STEM Innovation Center.
--boundary456
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="fullContent"

## REVOLUTIONIZING EDUCATION THROUGH TECHNOLOGY

Katwanyaa High School has officially opened its KSh 50 million STEM Innovation Center, marking a significant milestone in our commitment to 21st-century education.

### FACILITIES INCLUDE:

**1. Robotics & AI Lab**
- 20 programmable robots
- AI programming workstations
- Drone technology station
- Internet of Things (IoT) kits

**2. Digital Media Center**
- Professional recording studio
- Video editing suites
- Graphic design workstations
- Photography studio

**3. Science & Research Labs**
- Advanced chemistry laboratory
- Physics experimentation zone
- Biotechnology section
- Environmental science station

**4. 3D Printing & Design Studio**
- 5 industrial 3D printers
- CAD/CAM software
- Prototyping materials
- Product design stations

**5. Digital Classrooms**
- Smart boards in all rooms
- High-speed Wi-Fi (1Gbps)
- Video conferencing facilities
- E-learning platforms

### FUNDING PARTNERS:
- County Government (KSh 25M)
- Ministry of Education (KSh 15M)
- Safaricom Foundation (KSh 5M)
- Alumni Association (KSh 5M)

### GOVERNOR'S REMARKS:
"This STEM center positions Katwanyaa High School as a regional leader in technology education. Our students will now have access to facilities that rival top international schools."

### TRAINING PROGRAM:
The center will offer:
- Weekend coding clubs
- Holiday STEM camps
- Teacher training programs
- Community outreach sessions

The facility is open to students from 7:00 AM to 9:00 PM daily, including weekends for special programs.
--boundary456
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="date"

2026-04-18
--boundary456
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="category"

infrastructure
--boundary456
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="author"

ICT Department
--boundary456
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="featured"

true
--boundary456
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="stem-center.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< /path/to/your/image.jpg
--boundary456--

### 3. GET ALL NEWS (Test after creation)
GET {{baseUrl}}/news
Content-Type: application/json

### 4. GET SINGLE NEWS (Replace :id with actual ID)
GET {{baseUrl}}/news/1
Content-Type: application/json

### 5. UPDATE NEWS (Replace :id with actual ID)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/news/1
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=update123

--update123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Updated: Katwanyaa Breaks KCSE Records Again!